1. `How to find a number x in the array if it exist` : create iterator `it` and assign where `find` 
    pointing in the array for x , it will either point on very first occurrence of x or point at end
    then put condition if != d.end() then use `distance` this will return index using our iterator it.
    
    int x;
    cin >> x;
    auto it = find(d.begin(),d.end(),x);
    if(it != d.end()){
        cout << distance(d.begin(),it) << '\n'; 
    }
    else{
        cout << -1 << '\n'; 

    }
    
    
2. `Printing all elements of a array in shorter way` : this auto & will create c as iterator which will go from
    d.begin() to all way d.end() and print all elements which are present in the array d , this auto will manage
    all things own its own . 
    	for(auto & c :d){
    cout << c << ' ';
   }
   
   
3. `Finding smallest number in the array along with its index` : there are two ways to do this 

    	1. `First way` : `mn` is the variable which store the smallest number and `mni` will store index of number assigned
    	to mn , first initialize mn to the maximum possible valuable as per the constraints given and then in the loop when
    	you are taking inputs check if `mn > d[i]` then assign d[i] to mn and mni to i. 
    
    		int mn = 100000000;
   int mni = 0;
   for(int i = 0 ; i < n ;i++){
        cin >> d[i];
        if(d[i] < mn){
            mn = d[i];
            mni = i;
        }
   }
   
   	2.  `Second Way` : In this we created a iterator it and then used `min_element` builtin function and then this will point to 
   	the very first smallest element from the array and then we used `distance` this takes iterator and return int , this will 
   	find index of that number . Both approaches are efficient just this second one is little shorter . 
   	
   		auto it = min_element(d.begin(),d.end());
   int mini = distance(d.begin(),it);


4. `Printing N numbers of Fibonacci Sequence` : Fibonacci sequence is a such sequence whose first element is always 0 and second 
    element is always 1 and then from third elements all elements will be sum of precedding 2 elements sum like 3rd element 
    (2nd element + 1st element) . First create a empty array vector and then for i == 0 and i == 1 pushback 0 and 1 respectively
    and then `d[i-1]+d[i-1]` . 
    
    vector <int> d;
   for(int i = 0 ; i < n ;i++){
        if(i == 0){
            d.push_back(0);
        }
        else if(i == 1){
            d.push_back(1);

        }
        else{
            d.push_back(d[i-1]+ d[i-2]);
        }
   }
   
   
5. `reversing a vector array` : reversing will reverse array and not make array in descending order , use `reverse` this is builtin
    function will reverse our vector array . 
        reverse(d.begin(), d.end());
        
        
6. `Making copy of a vector array` : make sure if you taking input in a array and then wanted to copy that array then write `vector<int> 
    di = d` only after d's elements are initialized with the required input also make sure both vectors data type inside `<>` is same. 
    
    vector<int> d(n);
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        cin >> d[i];
    }
    vector<int> di = d;
    
    
7. `Bubble sort` : this is a algorithm which is used to sort a list of elements like array of numbers , but in modern versions of c++ 
    this is not preferable first its time complexity will very high high for more numbers and we have builtin `sort` function
    for.
    `Explaination` : We will swap any number only and only if it is greater than its adjacent element and we made a bool swapped that means
    if that is not greater than any adjacent then just break . 
    
    bool swapped;
    for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++)
    {
        swapped = false;
        for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++)
        {
            if (d[j] > d[j + 1])
            {
                swap(d[j], d[j + 1]);
                swapped = true;
            }
        }
        if (swapped != true)
        {
            break;
        }
    }
    
    
8. `Print the string _S_ from the beginning to the first '\'` : In this case we will use `getline` function to take complete input
    of the string  and then we will use `s.find('\\')` used double backslash to indicate one backslash and then we will create a
    substring from 0 to p , why not `p-1` because p is the number of characters we have to include in our substring starting from
    0 and we said p and numbering of the characters is always from 1 .
    
        string s;
  getline(cin,s);
  int p = s.find('\\');
    string r = s.substr(0,p);
    cout << r << '\n';
    
    
