12. `replace(s.begin(),s.end(),'a','b')` : replace is used to replace all occurrences of a particular character in a string 
    with any another character and in this example all occurrences of a will be replaced  with b.
    
    
13. `If wanted to switch case of the characters of a string` : Means if the particular character in a string is lowercase then
    convert to upper , then we will use `transform` and make sure to use `unsigned char` before `tolower` and to `toupper` 
    because toupper and tolower return in int but we want char. 
    
        transform(s.begin(),s.end(),s.begin(),[](unsigned char c){
    if(isupper(c)) return (unsigned char)tolower(c);
    if(islower(c)) return (unsigned char)toupper(c);
    return c;
   });
   
   
14. `Lexographical comparison between two strings` : First what lexogrpahical order is , this is the order which dictionairy
    use to sort things , like ab , ac then ab will come first comparing individual characters .  In c++ using lexographical
    comparsion could be done directly by using comparison operators consider a , b both as strings `a>b` if this is true then
    b will come lexographically first or we can say lexogrpahically small.
    
    
15. `swapping first character of two strings` : `swap(a[0],b[0])` this can be used to swap first character of two strings. 


16. `checking whether a string is pallindrome or not` : make a copy of original string and then reverse that copied string and 
    if `reversed of copied string == original string` then yes otherwise no
    
        string s;
  cin >> s;
  string r = s;
  reverse(r.begin(),r.end());
  cout << (s == r ? "YES" : "NO") << '\n';
  
  
17. `To count frequency of all letters present in a string ` : for this we will use hashing first create a array of 26 size 
    initialize all to 0 and then `d[i-'a']++` this will hash the frequency and then loop over d from 0 to 26 and if d[i] > 0 
    then print `i+'a'` this will give original character and `d[i]` this will give frequency , refer below example 
    
        
    string s;
  cin >> s;
  vector <int> d(26,0);
  for(auto &c :s){
    d[c - 'a']++;
  }
  
  for(int i = 0 ; i < 26 ; i++){
    if(d[i] > 0){
        cout << (char)(i+'a') << " : " << d[i] << '\n';
    }
  }
    
